AOSP path convention
====================

In the Android source tree, this sched-ext/scx repository should be the
project rooted at:

  external/scx/

So the Soong file in this repository is:

  external/scx/Android.bp   (i.e. ../Android.bp at repo root)

Do not add a second Android.bp under external/scx/ inside the same checkout:
that would appear as external/scx/external/scx/Android.bp when this repo is
already mounted at external/scx.

Generated Soong modules
-----------------------

`cargo_embargo` writes an `Android.bp` next to each Cargo package in this
workspace (see `cargo_embargo.json` at the repository root). The checked-in
files were produced with `run_cargo: false` (metadata-only) so they stay
compatible with current upstream `rustc`/`cargo` output; `cargo_embargo` from
AOSP should be refreshed periodically.

Regenerate locally (without a full tree, stub `bpfmt` on PATH that exits 0):

  export PATH="/path/to/stub-dir:$PATH"   # stub-dir contains executable `bpfmt`
  cargo_embargo --cargo-bin "$(dirname "$(which cargo)")" generate cargo_embargo.json

In a full AOSP checkout:

  cd external/scx
  m cargo_embargo
  cargo_embargo generate cargo_embargo.json

Manifest snippet
----------------

  <project path="external/scx" name="sched-ext/scx" revision="..." />

Compile check in AOSP
---------------------

After `repo sync`, add the project to your manifest (or use `git clone` into
`external/scx`), then from the Android tree root:

  source build/envsetup.sh
  lunch aosp_arm64-eng   # or another arm64 target
  m scx_lavd

`rustlibs` reference the platform `external/rust/crates` modules (for example
`libanyhow`, `liblog_rust`). If versions drift from this tree, re-run
`cargo_embargo` inside AOSP or adjust crate pins.

Note: enabling `"run_cargo": true` in `cargo_embargo.json` replays `cargo build -v`
through Soong’s parser; very new `rustc` flags can fail until `cargo_embargo`
is updated to match your toolchain.
